--- disjointes ou non
F: 
E: 
X: 
énumération: 
S (int, string): {i s}
Sh (scalaire, liste): {circle rect}
M (var : prudent): {a b} {a s} {b s}
pas une somme: ERREUR type is {disjoint?}: pt is not a sum
--- définitions
somme recouvrante : permise: 0
variante sans nom: ERREUR variant 1 of the sum has no name: a sum writes the name of its variant in its value; name it ({int}name), or write a union with "|" if the value itself tells the alternatives apart
union disjointe: 1
union anonyme: 1
union recouvrante : refusée: ERREUR union: alternatives i and s can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
union int | double: {10 U3.i} {2.0 U3.d} {16 U3.i} {20.0 U3.d}
union int | string: ERREUR union: alternatives i and s can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
point | vecteur : refusée: ERREUR union: alternatives p and v can take the same value, so the value could not tell which one it is; a union must be disjoint. Write a sum with "," to tag the alternatives
point , vecteur : somme: 0
mélange , et |: ERREUR mixing "," and "|" at the same level: a sum (,) tags its variants, a union (|) does not; group the inner part
énumération en union: on onoff
variante produit à un champ: {double}r
{-strict} n'existe plus: ERREUR type def: {-strict} is gone: a sum (",") always writes its variant in its value (v 5), and a union ("|") must be disjoint, so nothing is ever guessed
{-deduce} n'existe plus: ERREUR type def: {-deduce} is gone: a sum (",") always writes its variant in its value (v 5), and a union ("|") must be disjoint, so nothing is ever guessed
--- somme : la valeur écrit sa variante
nue : refusée: ERREUR value "5" names no variant of the sum S: a value of a sum is the name of its variant, then its value, as {i 5}, or {i:}5
{i:}5: {i 5} S.i
{S.s}5: {s 5} S.s
en clair: {s 5} S.s
par la chaîne: S.s
variante inconnue: ERREUR S has no variant "z" with a value
charge invalide: ERREUR expected integer but got "abc"
type {S.i}5: S.i
type cast S.i 5: S.i
type cast S 5: ERREUR value "5" names no variant of the sum S: a value of a sum is the name of its variant, then its value, as {i 5}, or {i:}5
type cast S {i 5}: S.i
point, vecteur: {v {1.0 2.0}} PV.v 1.0
littéral seul: vide Lit.vide
littéral : n 4: {n 4} Lit.n
variante typée nue: ERREUR value "4" names no variant of the sum Lit: a value of a sum is the name of its variant, then its value, as {n 4}, or {n:}4
--- lire
v(i): 5 int
expr {$v(i) * 2}: 10
expr {$v * 2} : refusé: ERREUR cannot use a list as left operand of "*"
lassign: i 5
type variant: s
type variant littéral: vide
type variant, pas une somme: ERREUR type variant: the value is a pt, not a sum
variante inactive: 5
f(rect.w): 2.0
f(w) : la charge courante: 2.0
f(zz): ERREUR prod<w:double;h:double;> has no field "zz"
--- la variante est dans la valeur
égalité: 0
clés de dict: 2
liste par la chaîne: S.i S.s
lappend {s:}x: S.i S.s
lappend en clair: S.i S.s
lset {s:}x: {s x}
produit: {{s 5} 3} S.s
retour de procédure: S.s
somme imbriquée: {k {s 5}} S.s
--- modifier
set v 8 : refusé: ERREUR value "8" names no variant of the sum S: a value of a sum is the name of its variant, then its value, as {i 8}, or {i:}8
set v(i) 8: i 8
set v(s) x : change: s x
incr v(i): i 6
--- union : la valeur est la charge
n: 5 U.n n
paire: {3 4} U.paire paire
u(paire): 3 4
expr direct: 10
étiquette qui confirme: U.paire
étiquette fausse: ERREUR value "3 4" is not valid for that variant of U
rien ne passe: ERREUR value "abc" matches no variant of U
--- casts
énumération -> string: rouge
somme -> string : son texte: i 5
somme -> int : refusé: ERREUR a value of the sum S is not of type int: it is "i" then its value; read that value by its path, as $v(i)
union -> int: int
union -> list.int: list<int>
int -> S : deux variantes ?: i 5
int -> F: {n 5} F.n
proc {string} <- énumération: vert
proc {int} <- somme: ERREUR argument "n": a value of the sum S is not of type int: it is "i" then its value; read that value by its path, as $v(i)
proc {int} <- v(i): 5
--- options et questions
{-compact}: 
sur une liste: 
inconnue: ERREUR type def: unknown option {-bof}: must be {-compact}
{-compact,-compact}: 1
alias: 
question inconnue: ERREUR unknown question "zz?": must be compact?, disjoint? or union?
